WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.335
-Our next guest is a talented
actress you know from her work

00:00:03.335 --> 00:00:05.204
on shows such as "Mad Men"
and

00:00:05.204 --> 00:00:06.773
"Chilling Adventures of
Sabrina."

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.575
She stars in
"Swimming With Sharks,"

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:10.276
which is available on
the Roku channel.

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:11.677
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.677 --> 00:00:17.416
-There are stories of love

00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:24.957
inspiring success over
the most insurmountable odds.

00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:28.795
Empowering stories,

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:31.464
where we're not crucifying
one another,

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.832
but playing fair.

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:41.174 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:43.676
This...
[ Growling ]

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:46.112
...is not one of those stories.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:49.949
-Please welcome back to the
show, Kiernan Shipka, everybody.

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.084
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.084 --> 00:00:58.257 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:58.257 --> 00:01:04.397 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.499
How are you?
-Hello! Oh, my goodness.

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:09.135
I'm well. How are you?
-I'm doing very well.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.403
-It's been so long.
-It's lovely to have you here.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.739
Last time you were here, we were
talking about "Sabrina."

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.240
-We were.
We were chatting 'Brina.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.509
-And this is now --
this is a lot darker

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:18.845
than the world of 'Brina.
-Ooh, I know.

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:21.581
Not a witch anymore.
-Not a witch anymore.

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:24.784
But somehow not a witch --
so it takes place in Hollywood,

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.219
and it's way darker than
witchcraft.

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:27.687
-Yeah, yeah, way more evil.

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:30.390
-So you play an intern
who's working for a sort of

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.258
high-powered Hollywood
executive.

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:33.426
-I do.

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:35.728
-Do you like the darkness of
this material?

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:36.996
-I love it.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:40.733
I don't know if I gravitate
toward dark material

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.502
or if it just finds me.
-Yeah.

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:46.739
-But it's my favorite to do.
I love being stoic.

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:49.108
I love having a secret.
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:50.442
And you do have a secret
in this.

00:01:50.442 --> 00:01:53.379
-Yeah, she's got a lot of stuff
going on up here.

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.547
-Yeah.
-Less dialogue than Sabrina.

00:01:55.547 --> 00:01:58.184
I was coming off of 10 months
of a ton of exposition

00:01:58.184 --> 00:01:59.652
and saving the world.
-Yeah.

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:00.953
And Sabrina had to do
a lot of spells.

00:02:00.953 --> 00:02:02.755
-She did.
A lot of Latin.

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.557
-A lot of Latin work
for an actor,

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.959
never fun to have to learn
Latin spells.

00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:09.462
-No. No.
That's not what you sign up for.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:11.297
-Exactly.
-But you do it anyway.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:12.598
-You do it anyway.
-Yeah.

00:02:12.598 --> 00:02:16.702
-And the other --
speaking of secrets, you know,

00:02:16.702 --> 00:02:18.604
I was first introduced to you
in "Mad Men."

00:02:18.604 --> 00:02:19.972
And the thing about "Mad Men"
that was interesting is

00:02:19.972 --> 00:02:22.508
I feel like all the adults
in the show had secrets.

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:24.109
You probably didn't have many
secrets in that show.

00:02:24.109 --> 00:02:26.645
-As a person, not as Sally.
-As a character, yeah, yeah.

00:02:26.645 --> 00:02:30.716
-Yes, also, yeah,
as a character.

00:02:30.716 --> 00:02:33.753
Yeah, she was learning
everything for the first time.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:35.221
-A lot of people, I feel like,
during the pandemic

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:37.290
went back and watched that show.
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.692
-Were you one of those people?
-I was, actually.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:42.328
-Okay.
-It was probably the first time

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:46.499
I truly sat down and binged
the whole thing.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.735
-I mean, it makes sense.
-I watched "Sopranos" first.

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:49.769
-Okay.

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:51.270
-And then I thought,
"What next?"

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.105
-Yeah.
-I guess, "Mad Men."

00:02:53.105 --> 00:02:55.574
And I did it.
-I mean, it makes sense.

00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:57.843
You weren't really --
it was not a show that was,

00:02:57.843 --> 00:02:59.679
like, age-appropriate for you
when you were starring in it.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:02.815
-No, no, not for 6-year-olds.
-Yeah.

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:05.051
Everybody says
you want to be like, 8

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:06.719
before you start "Mad Men."

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:08.253
-Honestly, 12, I think,
is the sweet spot.

00:03:08.253 --> 00:03:09.689
-Yeah, 12.

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:11.691
That's good that you can now
speak to it and be like, "12."

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:13.259
-Exactly.
But it was great.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:17.029
I felt like I was watching it
and I'm a fan of the show.

00:03:17.029 --> 00:03:19.298
-Did you ever, like,
forget something

00:03:19.298 --> 00:03:21.333
that you had done on the show?

00:03:21.333 --> 00:03:22.702
Like did you see yourself
in a scene?

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:24.737
-My memory was jogged. My memory
was always kind of jogged.

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:27.874
And I would sort of have an
association with the day, too.

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:29.875
-Yeah.
-I would say,

00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:34.814
"Oh, I had that sort of moment
outside of set after I --"

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:36.716
-That's a cool thing,
to be able to revisit that

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:37.884
and find that stuff.
-Yeah.

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:40.887
-On this show,
playing an intern,

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:43.456
sort of Hollywood
assistant world.

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:45.258
-Yeah.
-A lot of being on calls,

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:46.592
being on e-mails.
-Right, right, right.

00:03:46.592 --> 00:03:48.961
-Are you, in real life,
are you an organized person?

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:50.630
-No, I've got 3,000 e-mails
in my inbox.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.732
-No!
-Yeah.

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.133
[ Laughter ]
-No!

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:57.503
-And a lot of unread texts.
But something horrible happened.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:59.205
I learned that I had read
receipts on,

00:03:59.205 --> 00:04:01.407
and I didn't know that I did,
so --

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:04.243
-Oh, God. So for, like, years,
people have seen it?

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:07.280
-I don't know how long, Seth.
I don't know.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.581
-Well, if you don't remember
turning it on,

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.849
that means it's probably
always been on.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:12.117
-It could have been.
It's really bad.

00:04:12.117 --> 00:04:13.886
But, no, I have a lot of e-mails
in my inbox

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:16.189
that are not answered.
-That's alright.

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:17.556
-But a lot of them
are just spam.

00:04:17.556 --> 00:04:19.725
A lot of them are from, like,
a protein bar.

00:04:19.725 --> 00:04:21.427
-Yeah, some of them are probably
from family.

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.762
-Close, close family, yeah.
-Yeah, or emergencies.

00:04:23.762 --> 00:04:25.064
-Emergencies, yeah.

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:27.032
-Things that I should really
respond to.

00:04:27.032 --> 00:04:30.636
-I have heard tell that your
grandmother is very invested

00:04:30.636 --> 00:04:32.271
in her social media life.

00:04:32.271 --> 00:04:33.639
-She's big on it.

00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:38.378
She was very mad when Instagram
started hiding likes.

00:04:38.378 --> 00:04:40.513
-Okay.
-Because that was a really big

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:42.848
source of joy,
was when my photos --

00:04:42.848 --> 00:04:44.550
she would tell me
which photos were doing well.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.753
-Gotcha.
-And which were not.

00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:48.087
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:49.889
-So she would post
a photo of you?

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:51.891
-No, she would look at mine.
-Oh.

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:53.793
-And she would see how much
engagement they were getting.

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:55.394
-That's great.

00:04:55.394 --> 00:04:56.896
-Just to keep tabs on it,
I guess.

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:59.065
-That's better than if your
grandmother was out there,

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:01.367
like, posting her own stuff.
I think that's really adorable.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:02.835
-I think she kind of has
a burner account.

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:05.204
I don't think she posts anything
for herself.

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:06.505
-Very advanced,
for your grandmother

00:05:06.505 --> 00:05:08.474
to have a burner account.
-Exactly.

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:10.509
Yeah, I don't think she's
publicizing her life.

00:05:10.509 --> 00:05:14.213
-This is not a member of your
family, but I believe someone

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:18.518
as close as family is
Timothée Chalamet.

00:05:18.518 --> 00:05:20.352
-Ah, yes, Mr. Chalamet,
we love him.

00:05:20.352 --> 00:05:24.056
He's like family.
He's like an honorary Shipka.

00:05:24.056 --> 00:05:26.525
-How did he come into
the Shipka clan?

00:05:26.525 --> 00:05:30.729
-Into the Shipka-verse?
We did a movie together.

00:05:30.729 --> 00:05:32.532
-Okay.
-When I was 14,

00:05:32.532 --> 00:05:35.768
and he must have been maybe 18
at the time.

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:38.737
-Okay.
-And ever since then,

00:05:38.737 --> 00:05:40.973
has just kind of been, like,
a bro.

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:44.243
Sometimes would stay at our
house in L.A.

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:45.845
when he didn't have
a place to stay.

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:47.045
My mom would drive him to
auditions.

00:05:47.045 --> 00:05:48.881
-That's very nice.
-Yeah.

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:51.717
Back in the day.
Back in the day.

00:05:51.717 --> 00:05:53.318
-He's got a license now,
I heard.

00:05:53.318 --> 00:05:55.154
-Yeah, exactly.
He is driving.

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:56.255
-Things are going pretty well
for Chalamet.

00:05:56.255 --> 00:06:00.626
-And a direct offer or two
as well.

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:04.363
-Is it true that you once
brought him on a date,

00:06:04.363 --> 00:06:05.765
you third-wheeled him on a date?

00:06:05.765 --> 00:06:07.700
-Well, okay,
so here's the thing.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.501
It was sort of a date.
It was a lunch.

00:06:09.501 --> 00:06:14.539
It was a lunch with a boy,
and I didn't necessarily know

00:06:14.539 --> 00:06:17.142
what the vibe was yet,
so I wanted to bring a friend.

00:06:17.142 --> 00:06:18.844
-Uh-huh.
-And Timmy was the only person

00:06:18.844 --> 00:06:21.380
around, so I brought him.
-Gotcha.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:25.518
-Which, in hindsight, is maybe
not the most polite thing to do,

00:06:25.518 --> 00:06:28.553
because I do think the other boy
might have

00:06:28.553 --> 00:06:29.889
liked me a little bit.

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:31.991
-Well, he's probably has
e-mailed you about it.

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:33.159
-Yeah, I know.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.159 --> 00:06:34.360
-It's just waiting there
to be read.

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:37.363
-I wouldn't know.
I wouldn't know. Don't ask me.

00:06:37.363 --> 00:06:39.365
-Exactly.
-Yeah, it's deep down in there.

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:41.667
-Yeah, deep down.
That's just a lost message.

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:43.869
-I know.
-Hey, it's always so great

00:06:43.869 --> 00:06:45.337
to see you.
-Thank you.

00:06:45.337 --> 00:06:46.939
-Congratulations about the show.
Come back again soon.

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:48.073
-Anytime.

00:06:48.073 --> 00:06:49.741
-Kiernan Shipka,
"Swimming With Sharks"

00:06:49.741 --> 00:06:51.009
is available on
the Roku channel.

00:06:51.009 --> 00:06:53.079
Be right back with music
from Fontaines D.C.

